    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A kit wind turbine about 250 m off, seen from a low eye. The tapered white tower is raked from the left and has a base door, a gravel pad and a small pad mount transformer at its foot. Three twisted blades run off the top edge. A second turbine stands far off under the veil on the left, and the caliche road with its straw grass verge and barbed wire fence runs off to the right.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline, a reader sees one utility wind turbine on flat, empty Caprock ground at last light, with a county road beside it and open dark pasture across the road. That sets the place the deal is about before any figure appears.",
        "weakness": "Minor. The pasture's barbed wire fence, which the deck's motif starts here, is a row of hairline posts at the far right edge and does not register at feed size. The dark left half of the ground is a featureless wash under the type. The tower, nacelle, blades, base door and pad are finished at 100 percent and the base meets the ground with contact.",
        "repair": "none required",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
        "feed_legible": true,
